The Company’s four reportable segments are:

• the Data Center segment, which primarily includes server CPUs and GPUs, DPUs, FPGAs and Adaptive SoC products for data centers;

• the Client segment, which primarily includes CPUs, accelerated processing units that integrate microprocessors and GPUs (APUs), and chipsets fordesktop and notebook personal computers;

In addition to these reportable segments, the Company has an All Other category, which is not a reportable segment. This category primarily includes certainexpenses and credits that are not allocated to any of the reportable segments because the CODM does not consider these expenses and credits in evaluatingthe performance of the reportable segments. This category primarily includes amortization of acquisition-related intangibles, employee stock-basedcompensation expense, acquisition-related costs and licensing gain.

